<div class="prose">
  <p>The question I keep returning to is how a machine remembers, how it finds what it remembered, and how the two turn into thinking. This site is where I work on it in the open.</p>

  <h2>How I work</h2>
  <p>I start from a plain question, often a vague one and usually a “what if”. Then I stay with it: I read around it, write down what I think, work through the mathematics, and build the smallest experiment that could tell me something. Everything goes into the <a href="/notebook/">notebook</a> with a date, so the path from question to result stays visible.</p>

  <h2>Interests</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Memory in neural systems: storage, retrieval, and association</li>
    <li>Recurrent and associative memory</li>
    <li>Dynamical systems and the mathematics of learning</li>
    <li>The architecture of agents: what an agent is made of, and whether there is anything like System 1 and System 2 inside one</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Background</h2>
  <p>I build agentic systems, reinforcement-learning environments, and 3D and generative pipelines; some of that work is under <a href="/experiments/">experiments</a>. I came to AI from filmmaking.</p>

